_publ_section_comment
;
Rutile, titanium dioxide, TiO2

Each Ti ("A") atom is octahedrally coordinated by six O ("X") atoms. The 
resulting structure can be visualized in terms of edge-sharing octahedra,
 arranged in chains parallel to the crystallographic z-axis. Octahedra of 
neighbouring chains share corners.

Crystal structure listed in: Wyckoff, Crystal Structures (John Wiley, New 
York).
;
